BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:161548@iso-ne.com
DTSTAMP:20261109T153449Z
DTSTART:20261110T180000Z
DTEND:20261110T210000Z
SUMMARY:2026 Open Meeting of the ISO Board of Directors
LOCATION:Hilton Boston Back Bay\, 40 Dalton Street\, Boston\, MA 02115
DESCRIPTION:The purpose of this meeting is to conduct an open meeting of the ISO Board of Directors to give the public an opportunity to observe the Board’s discussions firsthand.\n\nThe meeting will be held both in-person and virtually. After the meeting\, the ISO will post a video recording for the benefit of members of the public who are not able to attend the meeting live. \n\nAdditional details\, including public transportation options\, can be found on the event website.\n\nIn-person registration closed on November 4.\n\nVirtual attendance is not limited and registration is not required. To attend this meeting virtually\, please join from the WebEx link below.\n\nWebEx link: https://iso-newengland.webex.com/iso-newengland/j.php?MTID=m65bdc3227aace0b87e3309f35e3adfa4\n\nPassword: ISOBoard2026!\n\nMeeting Number: 2439 478 0409\n\nThe meeting will include a Listening Session to provide an opportunity for both in-person and virtual attendees to address the Board directly. A limited number of timeslots are available.\n\nAnyone can submit written comments to the ISO Board of Directors either in advance or after the meeting. Please submit written comments by email to BoardofDirectors@iso-ne.com.\n\n\n	Written comments provided by Nov. 30 will be compiled and posted to the ISO website.\n\n\nIf you have any questions\, please reach out to Melissa Winne or Eric Johnson.\nhttps://www.iso-ne.com/event-details?eventId=161548
URL:https://www.iso-ne.com/event-details?eventId=161548
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:161793@iso-ne.com
DTSTAMP:20261109T153449Z
DTSTART:20261111T050000Z
DTEND:20261112T045900Z
SUMMARY:Veteran’s Day
DESCRIPTION:ISO New England observes this holiday:\n\n\n	Participant Support and most other departments are not staffed\n	Settlements will not be released and initial settlement metering deadlines will not fall on this day\n	The Credit department is closed\, along with Federal Reserve and BlackRock\n\n\nFor after-hours business emergencies\, contact Participant Support at (877) 226-4814 (pager). See Contact the ISO for other options.\nhttps://www.iso-ne.com/event-details?eventId=161793
URL:https://www.iso-ne.com/event-details?eventId=161793
END:VEVENT
